Package: SpatialEffect2
Type: Package
Title: Design-Based Inference for Spatial Treatment Effects
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ye", "Wang", email = "yw1576@nyu.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Cyrus", "Samii", role = "aut"),
    person("Haoge", "Chang", role = "aut"),
    person("P. M.", "Aronow", role = "aut"))
Description: Estimates the Average Marginalized Effect (AME) curve for spatial
    experiments under unknown interference, as described in Wang, Samii, Chang
    and Aronow (2024). The AME describes how treatment effects vary with
    distance in space. Supports point and polygon interventions, edge/disk/donut
    circle types, local polynomial smoothing with bias correction, Conley
    spatial HAC standard errors, and sharp null randomization tests. Built on
    the sf/terra spatial frameworks.
